  "notes": "N487AS also wears the oneworld scheme (Commons photo Anchorage 6 Jun 2025). N491AS is listed by Scramble.nl but not independently confirmed. Drawn from N486AS (left, 2026-02-19) and checked on N487AS (right, 2025-06-06): the aft sweep, fin and engines are Alaska's standard (2016) scheme; 'member of oneworld' and the gray Alaska title replace the standard navy 'Alaska' title. Registration in navy above the rear windows (not drawn). The wordmark's parts are titles of their own, so each side has its own set: on the right 'one' is aft of 'world' (N487AS, 2025-06-06). Re-checked 2026-11-15 (drawn on the 737-900ER, N486AS): the titles' lengths and places agree with the broadside 2026 photo; 'oneworld' is all lowercase, its x-height about 0.65 of the l's and d's height (recorded as xHeight, the title's height being the ascenders'); 'Alaska' lowercase about 0.55 of its A. The aft sweep is the standard's: its edges made smooth, with the silver-grey stripe ahead of the lime that the standard now has.",
  "from": "2021",
